  <data name="en_pano52_description"><![CDATA[<div>Welcome to Farin Ruwa Water Falls.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Located about 120 kilometres away from Lafia the state capital, and 30 kilometres away from Wamba the local government headquarters. The nature and beauty of the waterfalls take the breath away. The force of its gushing water is so torrential that it can be mistaken for white smoke, earning it the name “Farin Ruwa” a literal translation of “White water” in Hausa language.It is a truly magnificent work of nature incomparable with other waterfalls in Nigeria. This is because of its high level falls which is about 150 metres high and 50 metres wide. It is located Wamba Local Government Area of Nasarawa State.</div>]]></data>



  <data name="en_pano51_description"><![CDATA[As you approach the fall (about 100m) the roar of the fall becomes instance and very loud that you just have to shout for any one very close to you before you can be heard you. At about 50m – 70m to the base of the fall you will see and feel the cloudy mist generated by the fall, this in turn creates rain-like droplets as long the water falls, as the water rolls down the rock (about 100m) you will mistake it for a boiling water, the fall is so turbulent that you cant help it than to give kudos to mother nature, little wonder the United Nation named it as on of the world heritage sites. Visit Faring Ruwa (White Water) Falls (The 3rd largest natural Water Falls In the World) and experience nature at its best.]]></data>



  <data name="en_pano50_description"><![CDATA[As you approach the fall (about 100m) the roar of the fall becomes instance and very loud that you just have to shout for any one very close to you before you can be heard you. At about 50m – 70m to the base of the fall you will see and feel the cloudy mist generated by the fall, this in turn creates rain-like droplets as long the water falls, as the water rolls down the rock (about 100m) you will mistaking it for a boiling water, the fall is so turbulent that you cant help it than to give kudos to mother nature. Visit Faring Ruwa (White Water) Falls (The 3rd largest natural Water Falls In the World) and experience nature at its best.]]></data>



  <data name="en_pano49_description"><![CDATA[The trees found at this place are so tall (about 80m), casting a thick shadow at the forest floor that one can hardly see the sun, the sun ray cuts through the thick canopy, just like a golden sward and lights the forest floor. Walking through this beautiful flora, you are kept entertained by the chirping of assorted bird and the cry of monkeys.]]></data>



